  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lmi Consulting obligated $418M in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date, across 72 awards with an average award size of $5.8M. Lmi Consulting obligations are up 21.8% year over year. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, accounting for $214M, followed by General Services Administration with $109M and Department of Defense with $58.6M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the largest market, with $240M in obligations, followed by Engineering Services at $125M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. Award-value tables and expiring-contracts details are not included in these figures, so total contract values for largest awards or specific contract end dates are not available here. The mix of agencies and markets shows concentration in consulting and engineering work, with smaller pockets of R&D, landscape architecture, and office administrative services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Lmi Consulting's federal business trended this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Lmi Consulting obligated $418M in FY2026 to date, up 21.8% year over year. Lmi Consulting received 72 awards so far, with an average award size of $5.8M. Lmi Consulting obligations rose from $343M in FY25 to $418M in FY26, reflecting growth compared with prior fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets drive Lmi Consulting's revenue?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer with $214M, followed by General Services Administration with $109M and Department of Defense with $58.6M. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services leads markets at $240M, with Engineering Services second at $125M. Lmi Consulting also has obligations in R&D ($20.1M), Landscape Architectural Services ($16.4M), and Office Administrative Services ($15.8M)."
      }
    ]
  },
